<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Masonite yr shr slips, div decreased.</title>
<headline>Masonite yr shr slips, div decreased.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     164.0	 vs    189.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  42.0	 vs    50.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   11.22	 vs    12.86</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   16.13	 vs    20.91</p>
<p>    Tax			  4.92	 vs    8.05</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    0.70	 vs    0.17</p>
<p>    Turnover		 220.52	 vs    192.70</p>
<p>Div payable April 4</p>
<p>on register March 14</p>
<p>Full name: Masonite (Africa) Ltd (building and construction)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said some economic sectors such as furniture remained weak. It said the high interest rates and the unlikelyhood of any reduction in the first half of this year contributed towards a poor outlook.</p>
<p>But it said it would benefit from increased building activity and exports.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
